Hanoi, February 11, 2018 (VNA) – Prime Minister Phan Minh Triet and his wife visited the University of Brunei Darussalam (UBD) on the morning of February 11, 2018, during their visit to Brunei Darussalam.
The University of Brunei is the largest higher education and scientific research center in Brunei, ranking third in the region's university rankings.
The University of Brunei is one of the symbols of Viet Nam &apos; s cooperation with Brunei in education and training.
The University of Brunei formally established a partnership with the FPT University of Viet Nam in July 2013, with English training as the main area of cooperation.
In addition to foreign languages such as English, French, German, Japanese and Korean, Brunei University also incorporates Vietnamese into its curriculum.
During the visit to Brunei University, the Prime Minister of the Government of Vietnam, Ms. Fan Minh Diem, and Ms. Nguyen Phu Trong held a discussion with students of the Vietnamese language class.
Prime Minister Fan Minh Diệm is pleased that more and more foreigners are interested in learning Vietnamese and are making a positive contribution to promoting Vietnamese cultural characteristics and the image of Vietnamese people around the world.
Prime Minister Phan Minh Triet expressed his confidence and hope that the Vietnamese language teaching staff at the University of Brunei will be strengthened; that students in the Vietnamese language classes will be increasingly interested in the Vietnamese language, will work hard to learn it, will be able to speak fluently Vietnamese at an early age and will become ambassadors of friendly and cooperative relations between the two countries.
Prime Minister Phan Minh Triet also took the opportunity to interact via video with Vietnamese students studying English at the FPT-UBD Global Centre in Da Nang, to learn about their learning experiences, especially during the pandemic.
Prime Minister Phan Minh Triet considered the cooperation between the FPT University of Viet Nam and the University of Brunei, and in particular the FPT-UBD Global Centre, as a vivid symbol of the educational cooperation between Viet Nam and Brunei.
It is hoped that the students of the Centre will make greater progress in their studies and contribute positively to the friendly and cooperative relations between the two countries.
In his discussions with the Minister of Education and the leadership of Brunei University, Prime Minister Fan Ming-jiang highly praised the achievements of the two countries in educational cooperation, including the cooperation between FPT University and Brunei University, and the initiative of Brunei University to include Vietnamese in the curriculum.
Prime Minister Phan Minh Triet hoped that the University of Brunei will continue to focus on ensuring the quality of Vietnamese language teaching and further expand the size of Vietnamese language classes.
The Prime Minister of the Government of Viet Nam, Phan Minh Triet, also highly appreciated the positive results of cooperation between the two countries based on the memorandum of understanding on educational cooperation signed in April 2014; he recommended that Brunei continue to provide more scholarships and effectively implement short-term exchange training projects such as the Global Discovery Programme and the Discovery Year.
Prime Minister Fan Minh Diem highly appreciated the establishment of the first branch of Brunei University in Southeast Asia in Vietnam; believed that the University's scale of development in the region and the world is growing stronger; and further expanded the cooperation with Vietnam's higher education institutions.
On this occasion, Prime Minister and his wife planted a memorial tree on the campus of the University of Brunei and left a message in the memorial book.
Prime Minister Fan Minh Diệm wished the University of Brunei continued progress, greater strength to contribute to the educational cause in Brunei, and deeper and broader cooperation with educational training institutions in Vietnam.
(continued)
The Vietnamese press
"Important engine of global recovery"-China News Network
“In response to the COVID-19 shock, the Chinese economy has demonstrated strong resilience.
Recent market expectations indicate that the international community is generally positive about China’s future development.
Julio Ríos, a renowned Spanish expert on China and honorary advisor to the China Policy Observatory Network, said in an interview with the newspaper that China's current epidemic prevention and control has entered a new phase, and the dynamics of economic and social development will be further unleashed.
Mr. Ríos said that China had responded to shocks from various unexpected factors with extraordinary economic governance experience and measures, which fully reflected its economic resilience and level of management.
China is firmly committed to expanding its openness to the world, and the internal driving force of economic development is increasing, with State-owned enterprises and private enterprises developing in synergy.
Every year, two national conferences are held in China, where the representatives discuss the national development plan, the hot issues of the people's life in the parliament, and consolidate the consensus, the hearts and minds of the people, and the wisdom to add strength to China's development.
Since the reform and opening up, China has achieved long-term high-speed development and is now entering a high-quality development phase.
The international community looks to China for wisdom and Chinese programs, and for China's development to bring new opportunities to the world.
Riose said that China is now making every effort to promote science and technology innovation and inject new momentum into economic and social development, "financial investment, talent development, and policy incentives, which keep China dynamic in the new five-year plan."
In Rio’s view, economic institutional reform is a daunting task for any country.
Under the leadership of the Communist Party of China, China has taken positive and proactive measures to stabilize the economy, both by leveraging the advantages of the market economy and the advantages of the socialist system.
The strategic basis for expanding domestic demand, strengthening financial support for the real economy, supporting the development of the private sector, small and medium-sized enterprises and manufacturing, adhering to innovative development, promoting employment, improving the income and living standards of the Chinese people, meeting the people's multi-level diversified consumption needs ... China is complete, accurate and comprehensively implementing the new development concept, striving to promote high-quality development, build a new development pattern, and will bring more growth opportunities to the world.
This year marks the tenth anniversary of the Belt and Road Initiative.
“A stable economic recovery from the pandemic is a common goal of the international community.
China &apos; s unleashed economic development potential will bring more benefits to the world and become an important engine for global recovery.
"Rios said he expects the joint construction of "Belt and Road" cooperation to continue to play its important role in improving the infrastructure level of countries and strengthening connectivity in all areas, and continue to unleash greater momentum.
The article was published on the website of the Madrid Post.
(People's Daily, reporter Yang Ying)
Fitness industry should get out of crisis of trust - China News Net
Another big gym with a thunderstorm?
Recently, the issue of protecting the rights of fitness members in well-known fitness facilities has attracted social attention.
After the Spring Festival, many members found that their store was not operating normally, and subsequently, rumors about the collapse of the runway caused panic among members, leading to the intervention of public security and the human resources and social services department.
Finally, an official from the concerned body came forward to respond and promised that it would do its utmost to safeguard the legitimate rights and interests of employees and members. This was what brought about the end of the storm.
The first reaction of many members is that the problem is not a big deal, because some stores in individual gyms have problems, they are temporarily closed, and consumers should be calm and wait for the problem to be solved.
The profound problem behind the fitness club member advocacy is the crisis of trust in the industry.
Traditional gyms in China are generally based on pre-payment, and “making money from users who don’t come” is the underlying logic behind their growth.
By acquiring cash flow through pre-sale of membership cards and opening new stores continuously, it appears to be cyclical but in fact is merely eating one’s seed corn, unable to establish a stable profit model.
Negative messages from industries such as gym running tracks have been frequently circulated, causing a strong shock to consumer confidence.
From a market perspective, gyms are certainly a good business, and they “make money.”
The fitness track, though up and down, has always been the focus of capital.
Many data show that the market is continuing to warm up, with the interest in areas such as cultural and physical consumption continuing to rise.
Specifically to the fitness market, with the steady improvement in the living standards of residents, the concept of healthy living is deeply ingrained in people's hearts, and the fitness industry can be developed.
The better the situation, the more the industry needs to focus on quality of development.
However, the individual institutions, blindly optimistic about the recovery of the fitness market after the crisis, have sounded the bell of the opening of the Xiangtou territory and invested a brain of financing in the construction of new stores.
It is undeniable that in recent years, many institutions have withdrawn from the epidemic, the industry has been rechartered, and strong companies have been selectively increasing their acquisition efforts, repositioning, and not a new opportunity.
But if the fitness market is to enter a virtuous cycle and move on a steady and long-term avenue of health, the industry must change its traditional model and change its business strategy.
Only by taking a firm approach and rebuilding consumer confidence and security can we truly win the market and win the future.
Instead of building new stores to capture the market, the fitness industry now needs more than to optimize the service, with high quality development to keep users.
First and foremost, it is through service that users will be retained.
Gyms are part of the service industry, its essence is to adhere to "user-oriented", to closely around the user's needs, focusing on the operation of the service quality upgrade.
Secondly, to improve user experience, it is necessary to rely on digital transformation.
For example, the Internet gym model, which is now popular, allows users to pay per session and choose their own venue.
At the same time, body data and movement data can be used effectively, and can also meet social needs, achieving a complete closed loop of services from online to offline.
With no private-school marketing, no huge annual fees, users’ concerns about the “run-way” of the gym decreased, and their confidence increased.
In addition, the possibility of a multi-business model is actively explored.
Today, sports consumption has moved from single-service to scene consumption, with gyms promising to be the new entry point for consumption, surrounding the necessary sports supplements and fitness equipment as peripheral products or will become new perks, offering consumers a richer choice.
Jiang Tianjiao
Buy high, get the difference!
Nanjing real estate market replicates the difference in price of the compensation of the rent - China News Network
Yangzhou Evening News (Jurnalist Ma Zhaobo) Yangzhou Evening News/Violet News reporter found in an interview on the 10th that the price of the mortgage agreement, which had not been seen for more than a decade, has returned to the Nanjing housing market. A property in Jiangbei New District claims that the mortgage price is compensated by the mortgage, and other properties are offered more than the previous discount before the sale, and developers are willing to exchange the house for the buyer and return the difference.
The "Guaranteed Value Agreement" conditions aren't few.
The building is called the Polyantsi Yuntai in the Jiangbei New District, and the housekeeper, Mr. Sun, told reporters that he had found a “statement” while looking at the building last weekend.
The developer of the building has committed to exchange the property and refund the difference to the buyer of the property if the discount on the other property in the project is greater than the discount on the previous purchase (limited to other unsold property of the same type, building, unit, property type as the property) for those who purchased the property between 1 February and 28 February, from the date of signing the contract of sale between the parties and the delivery of the corresponding property.
Mr. Sun said that the home consultant said it was actually a "price insurance agreement", the purpose of which is to make the buyer feel confident to go, not to worry about developing business discount promotion, "now afraid to buy it to reduce the price, go to the building to mess up no time, if not to mess up, it is really safe."
Many homebuyers also believe that “price guarantee agreements” are “a painkiller” for homebuyers, but not at a low price.
Ms. Chung, who is planning to buy a short-term home in Jiangbei, said that the housing stock for the guaranteed price is first of all the same type of home, and also in the same building, the same unit, and the buyer can compare the few housing stock, so the "threshold" is still quite high.
Some buyers also believe that it is difficult for buyers to maintain their rights because of the asymmetry of information and the fact that they can not exclude additional concessions when selling.
The possibility of staying the buyer to be observed
The reporter in Nanjing online real estate inquiry, the building in November last year, the head of two buildings of a total of 252 units of housing source of sale permit, the area of the house is 105 square meters, 114 square meters, 129 square meters, etc., all the furniture sale permit average price of 39,843 yuan / sq.
However, more than two months later, online real estate shows that the total number of unsold units in the building is currently 157, representing 62.3 per cent, of which 128 units in Building 8, representing 113 unsold units, and 44 units in Building 7, representing 124 unsold units, and the total number of deals in the project is only 33, representing only 13 per cent.
Market sources have reported that “price guarantee agreements” have also appeared in Nanjing in 2008.
In August of that year, the building on Huangshan Road, Hebei, Yongkang West Yard to attract the attention of buyers, introduced the Guaranteed Price Plan, the specific content of which is "the company solemnly promises that if the project's concessions are expanded within a year, the resulting difference, the company will refund the difference to the old owner."
Since then, in April 2011, nine other properties in Nanjing have also taken out part of their property commitments to pay the difference in price.
“The housing market is warming up, and it needs a shot of ‘stronger’ now.
Mr. Shen, a senior trader in the Nanjing real estate industry, said that “price guarantee agreements” are also one of the marketing methods of real estate companies.
He believes that today developers need more confidence than buyers, and that the introduction of a price-fixing agreement is actually giving them a boost.
As to whether buyers would be retained, he said that this depended on the impact of multiple factors, such as regulatory policies and loan thresholds, which remained to be seen at present.
China's rescue team continues to carry out rescue operations in Turkey and has rescued four trapped individuals so far - Xinhua News Agency
On February 10, the Chinese rescue team sent three operating teams and 45 rescue personnel to rescue a trapped person who was searching for a rescue in Turkey, according to the Ministry of Emergency Management website.
Two search and evaluation teams were dispatched to conduct an assessment of 15 buildings on Wudaobaizhou Street.
To date, four trapped persons have been rescued, five victims have been searched and life signs and risk assessments have been conducted in 25 buildings that have collapsed severely.
The rescue team will continue to carry out in-depth rescue operations, adapting the rescue force scientifically and according to the actual situation in the disaster area and the situation on the ground.
The rescue team obtained information on assistance requests through multiple channels such as embassies, local governments, and UN relief organizations, verified them through various means including online inquiries and on-site searches.
The Chinese Hong Kong Rescue Team was briefed on the current situation in the rescue environment and building collapses, and the search operation was jointly conducted.
The United Nations is currently jointly responsible for regional coordination with the Italian Rescue Team (SSC5). At the same time, three team members are participating in the work of the Regional Rescue Coordination Centre No. 5, communicating with many teams, including those from Italy, the United Kingdom, Serbia, Slovakia and Oman, and learning about the situation of the United Nations Rescue Organization and the national rescue teams.
The rescue team continues to strengthen safety management and team security, in accordance with the principle of unified command, safety first, strengthen safety control at the rescue site, strengthen the discipline requirements for rescue work, and clearly define safety precautions.
Continuous operation of the system of shifts and post-working to strengthen the security management of the camps.
The medical staff of the rescue team provides medical examination services to the team members on a daily basis, and strengthens the medical protection of the priority personnel. All the rescue team members are now in good health and are carrying out the elimination of the camp area.
After establishing their own camps, the logistics security team members built 26 field battle tents of four main categories, including command communications, equipment storage, medical cleaning, living accommodation and dog shelters, and secured more than 30 sets of field rescue equipment.
Kim Jong-un's wife is a cold-blooded witch
(July 11, 2017) North Korea held the 75th anniversary parade of the founding of the armed forces on the evening of December 8, and Kim Jong-un's daughter Kim Jong-un not only attended but also stood on the podium with her father.
The video, released on 9th, showed Kim Jong-un with her father, making several friendly faces and talking about her father, touching his face with her hands and even touching his chest, and the interactive pictures of the father and daughter were broadcasted all over the country.
However, the First Lady Lee Hsien Loong could only back away.
According to Korean news outlets such as Korea News, Kim Jong-un and his wife, Lee Se-joo, took their daughter Kim Jong-eun to dinner on July 7. Kim Jong-eun was rarely seen sitting in the middle of the parents’ seat C, but she was also on the podium with Kim at the 75th anniversary parade of the National Day of the Army the following night.
The “North Korean Central Television” (KCTV) released footage of the parade after the fact, revealing more scenes of father-son affection.
Kim Jong-un has faced his daughter several times on the chair, and the smiles on their faces have never gone away, and they are also talking in each other's ears. Kim Jong-un once held his father's two arms with his hands, and Kim Jong-un responded with a smile.
Other official media footage also showed Kim's mother, Ai, touching her father's face while sitting on the sofa with Kim Jong-un in the living room; she was holding hands while walking with her father and touching Kim Jong-un's chest.
And First Lady Li Keqiang has been forced to walk behind or sit aside, always a few steps away from her husband and daughter.
Korean media reports that Kim Jong-un has been increasingly exposed in the past three months since he first appeared in public on November 18, 2017, when he tested the Mars 17 missile, and this is his fifth appearance in public.
The official North Korean media used titles such as "my dearest son" and "my noble son" to refer to Kim Jong-un, and broadcast footage of Kim Jong-un repeatedly shouting his death oath to the white blooded while watching the parade from the stands.
These signs have raised doubts about whether Kim Jong-il has been internalized as the successor to the Kim regime, with the Washington Post analysing it as “a signal that Kim is pushing his high-school-aged daughter into succession.” However, some have suggested that such a judgment is premature, and that possibilities remain open with a son in Kim’s lap.
Xinhua Commentary: Promoting China’s modernization in the Chinese style is a systemic undertaking – Four Commentaries on Deeply Understanding President Xi Jinping's Speech at the Opening Session of the Seminar for Studying and Implementing the Spirit of the 20th CPC National Congress - CNTV
Beijing, Feb. 11 (Xinhua) -- The promotion of Chinese-style modernization is a systemic project -- Four points to understand the importance of the opening speech of Secretary-General Xi Jinping at the seminar on learning and implementing the spirit of the Party's 20th Congress
Xinhua News Agency commentator
“Promoting Chinese-style modernization is a systemic project that requires comprehensive consideration, systematic planning and overall advancement, and the correct handling of a series of important relationships, such as top-level design and practical exploration, strategy and tactics, integrity and innovation, efficiency and equity, dynamism and order, self-reliance and openness to the outside world.
At the opening ceremony of the seminar on the twentieth anniversary of the Party and the implementation of Xi Jinping's socialist ideas with Chinese characteristics in the new era, held for members, deputy members and key leadership cadres at the provincial and ministerial levels of the New Progressive Party Central Committee, General Secretary Xi Jinping scientifically grasped the principles of modernization construction, systematically and in depth clarified a series of important relationships that need to be addressed in practice, and provided scientific methodology for us to vigorously advance Chinese-style modernization.
The promotion of Chinese-style modernization involves all areas of the economy, politics, culture, society, ecological civilization, and other aspects of relations between the ruling party and the military, domestic and foreign affairs, and defense, and must be well planned, but also be courageous to reform and innovate, and continuously achieve overall progress.
To design an overarching strategy requires deep insight into the world’s development trends and accurate grasp of the common aspirations of the people. It also involves in-depth exploration of economic and social development laws to ensure that the planning and policy system reflects its timeliness, adheres to laws, and is innovative. The plan should be coherent both far and near, harmonize top-down with bottom-up, and coordinate content.
The promotion of Chinese-style modernization is an exploratory endeavor, and there are many unknown areas that need to be explored boldly in practice, and the promotion of the cause through reform and innovation should never be a matter of waiting for the sword or the stock.
The strategic question is a fundamental question of a political party, a fundamental question of a country.
To advance the Chinese-style modernization, we must strengthen the forward-looking nature of the strategy, anticipate the future and lead it with scientific strategies; strengthen the comprehensive nature of the strategy, focus on solving the major problems that affect the rise and fall of the Party and the nation &apos; s cause and move the whole body at once; and strengthen the stability of the strategy. Once the strategy has been formulated, it must be adhered to for a long time, taken to its full extent and well-done.
We must scientifically grasp the dialectical unity of strategy and tactics, combine the principled nature of strategy and the flexibility of tactics, and be flexible, adaptive and ad hoc in our decision-making, and take strategic initiatives in a context that is adapted to the situation, and that is dynamic and favorable.
The Chinese people are a nation of integrity and innovation.
In order to deal with the relationship between innovation and integrity, we must safeguard the essence, origin, roots and soul of Chinese-style modernization, firmly adhere to the Chinese characteristics, essential requirements and major principles of Chinese-style modernization and ensure the correct direction of Chinese-style modernization. At the same time, we must place innovation at the forefront of the overall national development, respond to the development requirements of the time, focus on solving major theoretical and practical problems, actively recognize changes and respond to changes, vigorously promote reform and innovation, continually shape new development dynamics and advantages, and fully stimulate the creative dynamism of the whole society.
Efficiency is an important basis for fairness, and fairness is a strong guarantee of efficiency.
We are pursuing the Chinese-style modernization, which aims to create greater efficiency than capitalism, while at the same time more effectively preserving social equity, and better achieving the balance, promotion and unification of efficiency and equity.
We will deal with the relationship between efficiency and equity, and will continue to achieve development for the people, development dependent on the people, and development results shared by the people, so that the results of modernization and construction benefit all people more and more equitably.
To advance China’s modernization model, it is necessary to handle the relationship between vitality and order, ensuring that society remains both dynamic and orderly.
We must integrate development and security, implement the overall national security concept, strengthen the national security system, enhance the capacity to maintain national security and firmly uphold the security of the national regime, the security of the system, the security of the ideology and the security of the priority areas.
China has taken greater account of security aspects in its development, enhanced national security through development and used development achievements to strengthen the basis of national security. It has also been able to create a security environment conducive to economic and social development, continuously stimulating development dynamism and achieving a positive interaction between high-quality development and a high level of security.
To advance China’s modernization model, we must both adhere to our own path and broaden our world perspective; we should also uphold openness to the outside world, continuously expanding the breadth and depth of China’s modernization model.
We must maintain our independence and self-reliance, and we must insist on placing national and ethnic development on the basis of our own strength. We must insist on firmly holding the fate of our country &apos; s development and progress in our own hands.
To continuously expand the high level of opening up to the outside world, to participate deeply in the division of labor and cooperation in global industry, to use domestic and international resources to expand the development space of Chinese-style modernization, to share development opportunities in mutual benefit and win-win, and to create a bright future together.
Follow the path to achieve far-reaching goals.
Under the strong leadership of the Party Central Committee, with Comrade Xi Jinping as its core, and under the scientific guidance of Xi Jinping &apos; s socialist ideas with Chinese characteristics for the new era, let us grasp the rules, act with perseverance, fully use our energy, initiative and creativity, correctly deal with a series of important relations, strive to achieve the new goal of comprehensive construction of a socialist modernized country, and continuously open up new territory for modernization in the Chinese style.
The United States and Japan reach defence consensus against the Chinese Communist Party
Asia - February 9, Philippine President Bongbong Marcos visits Japan and meets with Prime Minister Fumio Kishida.
The two sides reached a consensus on opposing the Chinese Communist Party &apos; s violations of the South and East Seas, and the Fiji-Japanese leaders issued a joint statement after the meeting, stating that they would carry out substantive defence exchanges by signing a trilateral defence agreement with the United States and opposing the Chinese Communist Party &apos; s hegemony policy.
According to Japanese media reports, Kishida hopes that this meeting will help Japan and the Philippines establish policies for dealing with the crisis in the Taiwan Strait.
Marcos Jr. visited China in early January and was awarded a $20 billion deal.
But since then, relations between China and the Philippines have not only not improved but have actually deteriorated.
Earlier this month, the Philippines signed an agreement with the United States to open more bases for the US military to ensure security in the South China Sea.
The newly added base is located 300 km from Taiwan and is also one of the closest to China.
If there is a crisis in Taiwan, US forces may launch operations from bases in the Philippines.
The Japanese media believe that now Japan, South Korea, Australia and even the Philippines are forming an axis with the US to build a bulwark in the Western Pacific against the Chinese-Chinese arcade to promote regional cooperation.
China encourages higher fertility rate to encourage sperm donation to universities high quality standards
On 9 September, the Yunnan Province Human Sperm Bank in China issued a notice to solicit sperm donors with a university or higher education or students who successfully donate 8 to 12 times to receive a subsidy of RMB 4,500.
According to today’s reports in the Taiwanese media, the message was searched for on Weibo that day, and prompted follow-up initiatives in many provinces and cities, including Zhejiang, Shaanxi, Hubei, Shandong, and Beijing.
According to a report in the Times of India, China encourages university students to donate sperm.
The highest threshold for sperm donation is in Beijing, where in addition to academic qualifications, a height of 170 cm or more, a decent five-legged toe, no apparent hair loss, and a nearsightedness of no more than 600 degrees are also required.
According to the report, the Yunnan Human Sperm Bank stated that sperm donors can receive a complete set of men's health tests worth 1,000 yuan, "especially sperm and chromosome tests, which most people have never done, and are important for understanding their fertility status."
The conditions for donation include being 165 cm or more tall, having a college degree or higher or being in school, having color blindness, having a genetic disorder such as hepatitis B and infectious diseases.
The report cited China Tianmu News as saying that the human sperm bank in Shaanxi province had printed a poster with the slogan “Paid sperm donation, unlimited glory,” calling on young people to respond to sperm donation and encouraging netizens to pass on the message, “letting love pass on.”
The price of sperm in Xinjiang is higher than in Yunnan, where the qualified donor receives 300 yuan in cash each time, and the donor who completes a certain number of sperm donations receives a subsidy of 5000 yuan.
The highest known price is in Beijing, where the maximum subsidized price is RMB 5,150.
"Funds E-account" is coming: the Securities and Exchange Commission authorized to develop all funds under the name of investors achieves aggregation and query - Economic Observation Network - Professional financial news website
Economic Observer reporter Chen Shan How difficult is it to aggregate account information due to the proliferation of fund purchase channels?
Always forgetting "the little gold piggy bank"?
These problems of the Ki-inhabitants are about to be resolved.
On February 10, the SEC announced that the "Fund E Account" APP was listed in various mobile application stores and conducted a public trial.
It is reported that "Fund E Account" provides one-stop query services for individual investors to obtain information on public offering fund accounts and shares, aiming to address industry pain points such as forgetting account numbers and querying them in a cumbersome manner.
According to Wind data, by the end of 2022, there will be 156 public equity fund managers in China, managing funds of about 26 trillion yuan; 167 public equity fund share registration agencies and 411 public equity fund sales agencies.
The accounting systems of the different quota registries are independent of each other and lack a unified industry-wide query channel.
According to industry experts, at the end of 2021, there were more than 720 million fund investors in China, which means that half of the country invested in fund products.
Previously, investors had to search for purchases through different sales agencies, but with the “fund E account” they can search for purchases through all sales channels, and have a clear view of the fund holdings.
What is the Fund E-Account App?
According to the relevant documents, the E-Account APP is a mobile application for the Chinese public fund industry portal for settlement in China approved by the China Securities Regulatory Commission for development and construction, which provides investors with a one-stop-shop inquiry about the holding of outstanding shares in the market of public fund products.
Investors can easily and quickly manage their holdings of off-the-shelf shares of publicly traded fund products under the management of various fund managers purchased through various sales channels throughout the market through "fund e-account", which improves the efficiency of querying.
Specifically, the information that investors can access through the Fund E Account includes information on fund accounts opened with publicly traded fund managers across the market, information on trading accounts opened with publicly traded fund sales agencies, and information on off-site shareholdings in products such as publicly-received portfolio investment funds and collective asset management plans that are managed by securities companies and have a maximum of 200 investors.
The Shanghai Securities Fund Evaluation Research Center business manager, Liu Yiqiu told Economic Watch Network reporters that investors can get a one-stop-shop information about all their holdings of OTC funds through the OTC fund E Account OTC App, which helps them find the forgotten asset pairs, and more importantly, the complete account information summary of the integrated fund investment situation for clients, which helps clients to better understand their investment situation in a timely, accurate and complete manner, thus better optimizing their portfolio fund configuration and better planning their financial arrangements.
How to register for use?
The reporters noted that at present, the "fund e-account" APP has been on the market in the Huawei, Apple, Xiaomi, OPPO, Vivo and other mobile app stores, but the APP is still in the public trial phase, registration requires filling out the invitation code, investors can contact the fund manager of the fund held.
A customer service representative of a large Shanghai-based public fund provided a six-digit invitation code to a reporter from Economic Watch and told reporters that during the test phase of the app, China is expected to provide a certain number of invitations to each fund manager, and investors will come and get them.
After the trial run, the invitation code will no longer be used for open user registration.
Translation requested.
The journalists according to the official website of the Securities and Exchange Commission published "fund E account" download and use instructions related documents to register the account and complete the query, the whole process takes only a few minutes, mainly divided into four steps: user registration, real name authentication, fund account binding, public fund query.
After this step, click on the button to link the fund with the real name, and all the fund products purchased by the journalist through the various fund sales platforms will be presented in the list of binding options ("binding accounts").
It is worth noting that the Fund E account only provides query services to investors and does not allow redemption transactions.
The data dates displayed in the Fund E account are generally three trading days ahead of the date on which the user requested the query (T-day).
For example, if a “fund E account” is opened on February 10, the assets page shows total assets, fund shares, and net fund value corresponding to the date three trading days ahead of that date, i.e., February 7.
