Multiple data points show poor start to year for Taiwan's economy - Xinhua News Agency
Xinhua, Taipei, February 11 (Reporter Zhao Bo, Huang Yang) Export trade amount "five black", manufacturing purchasing managers index (PMI) contracted for seven consecutive months, the consumer price index (CPI) again see "three heads"... Recently, the Taiwanese authorities have successively released economic data for January 2023.
Experts believe that the Taiwan economy has not performed well at the beginning of the year and that growth pressure is not negligible.
According to the Taiwan authorities' financial affairs department, Taiwan's exports in January this year amounted to $31.51 billion, down 21.2 per cent year-on-year, and negative growth for the fifth consecutive month.
The exports of 11 major export categories declined in comparison to the same period last year.
Plastic rubber and its products and optical equipment suffered the greatest decline, with a year-on-year decline of 37.6 per cent and 35.7 per cent, respectively.
The export of electronic components fell by 20.1% year on year, the largest decline in 11 years.
Of these, integrated circuits fell by 18.3 per cent annually, the largest decline in 14 years.
According to the department's statistics director, Ms. Kimena, this shows that the effects of weak demand in the consumer electronics industry are spreading and the electronics industry is entering a correction period.
Statistics show that in January, Taiwan's imports and exports doubled, with the exports exceeding only $2.34 billion, the lowest level in almost three years.
The Taiwan authorities' financial services department believes that global terminal demand is declining, industry adjusts inventories to suppress the willingness of manufacturers to purchase, and exports are unlikely to improve in the short term, and Taiwan's exports decline in the first quarter of this year is more likely than expected.
According to the Taiwan Institute of China Economics, the Taiwan Manufacturing Purchasing Managers Index (PMI) in January this year was 40.4% seasonally adjusted, down 3.3 percentage points from December last year, a seven-month consecutive contraction.
In the system of economic monitoring indicators, the PMI is 50% as the boom line, and an index greater than 50% represents expansion, and the opposite, contraction.
In January, the five components of the Taiwan PMI showed contracting new orders, production and employment, declining supplier delivery times and stock contracting.
The six largest industries reported total PMI contraction, with each industry ranked according to the contraction rate as the electrical and mechanical equipment industry ((35.1%); electron fluorescent optics industry ((35.2%); chemical and biomedical engineering industry ((39.2%); basic raw materials industry ((42.4%); transportation industry ((42.6%) and food textile industry ((45.7%)).
In terms of prices, the Taiwan authorities’ “Controller General Office” announced that the annual CPI growth rate in January this year was 3.04%, again breaking the 3% mark since July last year.
Among them, vegetables rose by 28.25 per cent, a new 17-month high.
According to Cao Zhihong, a special commissioner of Taiwan’s “General Comptroller’s Office,” the increase in vegetable prices is indeed higher than expected, and if the Spring Festival factor is excluded, the average CPI in January and February should be close to the 2.71% of last December, and inflationary pressures are still present and remain high.
In a comprehensive report on the Taiwan economy this year, based on local media reports from the United Press, Yahoo Finance and others, experts expressed pessimism.
Liu Daing, professor of the Department of Economics at Taipei Central University, said that the export recession could cause problems in the cash flow of export manufacturers and increase the risk of default.
At the same time, the reduction in orders has led manufacturers to reduce labour costs, affecting the labour market and household economies, which in turn impacts on consumer power.
According to the Taiwan Institute of Economic Research researcher, Chu Dasheng, the inflation situation in Europe and the United States remains unresolved this year, demand continues to contract, and the Taiwan export recession is expected to continue into the first half of the year.
As the Taiwan economy is export-driven and is affected by export slowdown, the overall growth performance will be lower than last year.
Did the Balloon Incident Brighten America's Eyes?
Strengthening restrictions on technology exports to China
The Wall Street Journal reported today that the United States is preparing to further tighten its technology exports to China after the balloon incident.
Current and former security officials have said that the balloon incident highlights the national security threat posed by China, and will seek more political support for strengthening US technology protection.
The US claims that the balloon carried antennas and sensors for intelligence gathering and communications.
According to Martyn Rasser, a former senior CIA official who now works at the Washington think tank's Center for a New American Security.
"This is undoubtedly a fuel for the fire, supporting the hardliners' views on China."
White House press secretary Karine Jean-Pierre told reporters Thursday that the U.S. will also consider taking broader action to expose and respond to China's larger-scale surveillance activities, which pose a threat to our national security and to our allies and partners.
The U.S. officials said they had notified the governments of more than 30 countries about the balloon incident and that international coordination was vital to counter the Chinese threat.
Emily Benso, a senior researcher at the Center for Strategic and International Studies, says that, in addition to the Biden administration’s actions, the newly formed House Committee on Strategic Competition between the US and the Chinese Communist Party may also put pressure on the US to take tougher measures to slow China’s development.
She said that Congressmen would feel increasing pressure to take a tougher position, which in turn might force the White House to adopt a tougher policy.
According to the Wall Street Journal, many advocates of tighter export controls are also pushing for the expansion of the controls to include industries such as artificial intelligence.
The US government has also been developing an outward investment review program to examine whether US investments abroad pose potential national security threats from China.
Analysts say the White House may face calls for a faster launch of the plan.
The first individual pension products have been launched, with minimum holding period of 360 days - Xinhua News Agency
The first personal pension products are on sale
The seven products of the institution are available for a minimum of 360 days.
The personal pension products are finally online.
On February 10, China Financial Network released the first list of personal pension financial products, seven of the personal pension financial products of the Industrial Bank of China, the Agricultural Bank of China and the Postal Bank of China were officially released.
The “shelf” of personal pension accounts now includes four types of products: personal pension savings, personal pension financing, personal pension insurance, and personal pension public fund.
It was described that the first set of personal pension products, all of which are public equity net-value open-ended products, of which five are new products, two are existing products, and except for one product is a mixed product, the remaining six products are all fixed-income products.
The Beijing Youth Reporter saw that four of the five new products were from the Industrial Bank of China, all of which are fixed-income products, with minimum holding periods of 365 days, 540 days, 720 days and 1080 days, respectively, and the corresponding performance benchmarks (annualized) are 3.70% - 4.20%, 4.10% - 4.60%, 4.40% - 4.90%, 5.25% - 5.75%, respectively.
The remaining new product is the Liang Post Bank Wealth Addition. Liang Jin holds the 1st position for a minimum of 1095 days. Liang, also a fixed income product, began the tender on February 10 and ended on February 19, with a risk rating of second.
The two products that are still in existence are the KARO Bank's financial and financial assets, the KARO Bank's 360-days of innovative technology and innovation in RMB, the investment nature of which is a hybrid category, and the risk rating is three.
The second ongoing product is “Post and Express Wealth Add Joy - Harmony Shortest Holding for 365 Days No. 1,” which is of fixed income type. It started fundraising on December 30 last year and officially began operations on January 4 this year. Its cumulative net asset value as of February 8 was 1.0011.
According to the opinion of the State Council Office on Promoting the Development of Individual Pensions, the financial products in which the funds of the Individual Pension Fund Account can be invested include banking, savings deposits, commercial pension insurance, public funds, etc.
The launch of the first personal pension product marked the official opening of the personal pension account for individual pension investors.
In November last year, the BPS developed the "Temporary Procedures for the Management of Personal Pension Businesses of Commercial Banks and Financial Services Companies."
The PPP provides that participants can purchase personal pension savings, personal pension management products, personal pension insurance products, personal pension fund products and other personal pension products through their personal pension fund accounts.
Subsequently, the Ministry of Human Resources and Social Affairs, the Ministry of Finance and the National Taxation Bureau issued circulars specifying that the personal pension system would be implemented in Beijing, Tianjin, and 36 pioneer cities and regions, including Shijiazhuang, the Yunnan New District and Jincheng City in Shandong Province.
By the end of 2022, the number of individual pension participants will be 19.54 million, and the number of contributors will be 6.13 million, with a total contribution amount of 14.2 billion yuan.
Previously, the banks participating in the pilot had only listed three types of products: personal pension savings, personal pension insurance products and personal pension public funds.
Now that personal retirement products are also available, what should investors choose?
The experts of the Research and Development Department of the Bank of Investments said that, compared with other personal pension products, the pension product in the pilot phase and the personal pension product have three characteristics.
The first is stability, better risk management mechanisms, more robust investment strategies and concepts, and the implementation of independent third-party custody outside the parent bank.
Second, the long-term nature of the product. The term of the pension products in the pilot phase is five years or more, and the next-stage issue of the personal pension product will have a minimum holding period of one year in principle, with an encouragement to hold for more than three years.
Third, the product is universal, with a low threshold for purchase, usually starting at 1 yuan, and some as low as 0.01 yuan, and the rates of the products &apos; custody fees, management fees, etc. are more favourable.
Experts point out that investors should make their choices based on the product's characteristics and their own risk tolerance.
Personal pension savings have long term, high interest rates and high security characteristics, and are suitable for people with low risk tolerance; personal pension insurance products are more secure and are more suitable for people who cannot take investment risks and can accept stable returns; while personal pension management products and public equity funds products do not provide insurance or returns, have a certain investment risk, but expect higher returns, and are suitable for people with a certain financial knowledge and a higher risk tolerance.
The article/Reporter of this newspaper, Chang-Yun, is published by the Chinese newspaper, Yue-Chang/Pike Haipo.
The 20th Seminar on the Implementation of Xi Jinping's Socialist Ideas and the Party's Spirit in the New Era for Members, Substitute Members and Principal Leaders of the Newly Elected Central Committee and Provincial-Ministerial-Level Staff is Completed - Hunan Daily News Network - Huasheng Online
The 20th Seminar on the Spirituality of the Party and the Implementation of Xi Jinping's Socialist Thoughts with Chinese Characteristics in the New Era was held for members, alternate members and key leadership cadres of the New Generation Central Committee at the provincial and ministerial level.
February 11, 2023 at 1:07 PM [Source: Xinhua News Agency] [Editor: Li Sufeng] Font size: 【large | medium | small】
Xinhua Beijing, February 10th, 2017 Members, alternate members and key leadership cadres of the Central Committee of the CPC Central Committee and provincial ministries studied to implement Xi Jinping's socialist ideas and Party's 20th Great Spiritual Seminar on China's New Era Characteristics in the Central Party School (National Administrative Academy) on the afternoon of February 10, with Secretary of the Standing Committee of the CPC Central Political Bureau and the Central Secretariat, Yang Qi, attending the closing ceremony and giving a concluding speech.
He said that the Chinese people should learn in depth from the spirit of the important speech of General Secretary Xi Jinping at the opening ceremony of the seminar, more firmly uphold the principle of "two establishments" and firmly do the "two defences", strengthen their skills, take serious action, and firmly advance the work of Chinese-style modernization, and achieve results that can be tested by history, practice and the people in the comprehensive construction of a socialist modernized state and the comprehensive promotion of the great revival of the Chinese nation.
During the seminar, all participants were guided by Xi Jinping's ideas of socialism with Chinese characteristics in the new era, carefully studied the spirit of the 20th Party Congress and the important speech of the General Secretary Xi Jinping at the opening ceremony of the seminar, and engaged in in-depth discussions and exchanges in connection with practical activities. They deepened their understanding of a series of major theoretical and practical issues of Chinese-style modernization, strengthened their confidence and determination to comprehensively advance the great revival of the Chinese nation with Chinese-style modernization under the strong leadership of the Party Central Committee, with Comrade Xi Jinping as its core, and strengthened their sense of responsibility and mission to fulfil their duties, do their work well and ensure a good start to the new era.
The closing ceremony was attended by 10 representatives of the seminar, who gave their reports and exchanged their knowledge and experience.
Mr. Cai said that learning to implement Xi Jinping's socialist ideas with Chinese characteristics and the twentieth spirit of the Party in the new era is both a primary political task of the present and future periods and a long-term strategic task. According to the requirement of "comprehensive learning, comprehensive grasp, comprehensive implementation," we must promote the learning and implementation work to continue to go deep, go to practice, and go to the heart.
We must understand more deeply the decisive significance of the "two establishments", firmly uphold the central position of Xi Jinping, uphold the central authority of the Party and centralize the unified leadership, continuously improve the political judgment, political understanding and political execution, and always maintain a high degree of consistency in ideas, politics and action with the Party Central Committee, which has comrade Xi Jinping as its core.
We must strive to master the basic knowledge of Marxist theory, consciously armed our minds with the Party's innovative theory, guide our practice and promote our work, and make every effort to study in depth, understand thoroughly and work with determination, truly learning to be firm in our convictions, learn absolute loyalty and learn to fulfil our mission.
We must implement the decisions of the 20th National Congress of the Party with a spirit of enthusiasm and commitment, firmly advance the Chinese-style modernization, roll up our sleeves and get ready, and act as a good "construction team leader" to turn the blueprint into reality step by step.
We must keep in mind that the comprehensive and strict control of the Party is always on the way, and the Party's self-revolution is always on the way. We must firmly implement the political responsibility of the comprehensive and strict control of the Party, and take the political construction of the Party as our guiding principle, and make a great stride forward in the new great project of building the Party of the new era.
We must strengthen the capacity to promote high-quality development, serve the people, and prevent and mitigate risks, and we must encourage research and research and firmly prevent and overcome formalism and bureaucracy.
Shi Taifeng, Li Ganjie, Li Shulei, Chen Wenqing, Liu Jinguo, Wang Xiaohong attended the graduation ceremony, and Chen Hi presided over the graduation ceremony.
The last Communist Chancellor of East Germany dies today
The successor of the East German Communist Party, the Communist Party of Germany, reported in a statement that "Hans Modrow passed away last night at the age of 95".
As a result, our party has lost an important leader.
Translation requested.
On November 13, 1989, four days after the Berlin Wall, which had separated East and West Berlin for 28 years, was opened, Mudros said he would help turn East Germany into a democracy.
At that time, the Communist Party leaders were forced to step down as protesters across East Germany demanded democracy and freedom.
After the Soviet Union came to power, Mikhail Gorbachev called for changes in Soviet-dominated Eastern Europe as well.
In March 1990, Möderndorfer declared the first and only free elections in the German Democratic Republic (GDR).
The election result led to his resignation as Prime Minister.
Despite Modr's reforms, opponents accused him of trying to delay the political change and unification that took place in October 1990.
He was also criticized for trying to rebuild, rather than abolish, the secret police.
In 1993, Modrow was convicted of electoral fraud in the May 1989 municipal elections, but he was not jailed.
These allegations were allegedly politically motivated.
From 1990 to 1994, Modrow continued to serve in the German Bundestag and from 1999 to 2004, he was a Member of the European Parliament.
Mudros sees himself as a reformer and wants to change the Communist Party from within.
In 1999, he told Reuters that he did not want the former East Germany to return, but that it should be recognized for its achievements.
Modrow was born in 1928 in the then German town of Jasenitz (now Jasienica in Poland) and trained as a mechanic.
During World War II, he served as a youth fire brigade leader and soon after the conflict ended as a member of the Volkssturm, a Nazi militia organization that recruited men aged 16 to 60 to fight in the final war struggles.
At the age of 17, Modrow was captured by the Soviet army and taken as a prisoner of war to the Soviet Union, where he attended anti-Fascist courses and became a committed Communist.
In 1949, the year East Germany was founded, he returned to his homeland and found a job as a mechanic, and continued his studies in social sciences and economics, obtaining a doctorate.
Modrow was a staff member of the Free German Youth Movement, which almost all East German youth joined, and was promoted to the position of president of the Dresden Regional Party from 1973 to 1989 through the ruling Social Democratic Union Party (SED).
He also served in the East German parliament for more than 30 years.
In 1990, Modrow became the de facto leader of East Germany and held the highest state office.
Hanoi, Vietnam – The official visit of Prime Minister Phan Minh Triet and his wife to Singapore and Brunei has been successful and has yielded comprehensive, practical and concrete results, according to the Vietnamese news agency VNA.
During the three days of her visit to Singapore and Brunei, PM Fan Mingyi has attended more than 30 different events.
The results achieved have provided new impetus for the further development of the new strategic partnership between the two countries and the Vietnamese Comprehensive Partnership in a deeper, broader and more effective direction.
During his visits to both countries, Prime Minister Pham Minh Triet continued to reaffirm the foreign policy of the Vietnamese Party and the State, namely, independence, autonomy, pluralism, diversity, willingness to be a good friend and reliable partner of all countries and a responsible member of the international community.
Strengthening relations with Singapore and Brunei is a need of the respective countries, which are committed to the welfare of their peoples and to peace, stability and development in the region and the world.
During the meetings and discussions, Prime Minister Fan Minh Diem and the leaders of Singapore and Brunei agreed to continue to strengthen political mutual trust with Vietnam through high-level delegation visits and effective implementation of bilateral cooperation mechanisms and important cooperation agreements.
Many cooperation documents were signed during the visit.
Two highlights were the Memorandum of Understanding on a Green and Digital Economy Partnership with Singapore and the Action Plan for Strengthening the Viet Nam-Brunei Comprehensive Partnership for the Period 2023-2027 with Brunei.
Vietnam and Singapore Sign Green and Digital Economy Partnership Memorandum of Understanding.
Image from the Vietnamese news agency
During meetings with business leaders, seminars or attendance at economic forums, PM Fan Minh Diem stressed that Vietnam welcomes and facilitates the expansion of investment in the fields of digital transformation, green energy, high technology, innovative innovation and other areas by Singaporean and Brunei enterprises.
The visit will not only help deepen Vietnam's cooperation with Singapore and Brunei in traditional fields such as politics, diplomacy, economy, security, defence, education, training, oil and gas, tourism, people-to-people exchanges, but also create a framework for cooperation in new potential areas such as the digital economy, green economy, energy transition, innovation, smart cities, sustainable development.
King Hassanal Bolkiah of Brunei and Prime Minister Phan Mạnh Quỳnh are preparing to enter into bilateral talks.
Image from the Vietnamese news agency
During his visits to both countries, Prime Minister Phan Minh Giang made time to visit and listen to the thoughts and aspirations of the local Vietnamese diaspora.
During the meetings between the two leaders, Prime Minister Phan Minh Triet recommended that the authorities of both countries pay more attention to and create favourable conditions for the local Vietnamese community to be treated fairly, to have the opportunity to contribute to local society and to foster bilateral relations.
The proposal has been agreed to and supported by both leaders of the two countries.
In particular, Prime Minister Fan Mingyi also shared with the leaders of the two countries the desire for a united, peaceful, stable and prosperous ASEAN community; agreed to maintain united cooperation with ASEAN countries and enhance the central role of ASEAN in the complex and changing context of regional and international situations.
With the important results achieved, Prime Minister Phan Minh Triet &apos; s official visits to Singapore and Brunei contributed positively to the effective implementation of the outward route of the Thirteenth Congress of the Communist Party of Vietnam, which prioritizes the strengthening of relations with ASEAN neighbours, the effective implementation of the Conclusion No. 12 of the Political Bureau of the Communist Party of Vietnam on the work of Vietnamese expatriates in the new situation (12-KL/TW) and the use of the strength of all-national solidarity.
(continued)
NEWS GOV-MO: Police announcement: Police Department calls on citizens to beware of fake telecom companies scam text messages
Recently, the Department of Police received several telecom fraud cases, criminals fake Australian Telecommunications Company to the owner of the fraudulent text message attached to the website link, with the credits expiring as soon as possible to redeem the prize as a bait, lure the owner to log into a fake website to redeem.
The owner entered the credit card details and the verification code as instructed and immediately received a notification from the financial institution that the credit card had an unknown consumption record and that the credit card details were suspected of having been stolen from the aforementioned website.
The investigation confirmed that the telecommunications company concerned had not sent the aforementioned text message.
The Police Department urges citizens to be vigilant if they receive such mobile text messages and not to click on the website links contained in the text messages or provide any personal information; if they are asked to provide credit card information, account transaction passwords, transaction verification codes, they should be extra careful to prevent credit card theft.
The following is a tip:
1. Pay more attention to cybersecurity information and raise personal awareness of prevention;
Do not casually log onto unknown websites and register your personal and credit card information there to prevent identity theft;
3. Be vigilant against fake and phishing websites and always check that the URLs of the websites are fully consistent with the official ones;
4. Install antivirus software for mobile phones, mobile devices or computers and update it regularly;
5. If suspected of fraud or other crimes, the police should immediately contact the Telephone Department's Anti-Fraud Hotline 8800 7777 or the Reporting Hotline 993 for assistance.
EU summit debates refugee policy, EU officials: reception process is a bottleneck - China News Network
EU summit overrefugee policy deadlock; EU officials say bottleneck at every step of admission process
According to AFP, on February 10, at the latest EU summit of the day, EU Commission President Jean-Claude Juncker said that EU leaders agreed to a stricter policy on illegal immigration, which would make it easier to deport illegal immigrants.
The EU’s move is reportedly in response to growing concerns about illegal immigration in Europe, where the core problem today is that few illegal migrants are eventually repatriated.
According to the summit document, EU leaders called on the Commission to immediately mobilize large amounts of EU funds to strengthen the external borders through infrastructure and surveillance.
However, the EU is in constant dispute with its member states over issues such as the payment of the fence fee.
Von der Leyen has repeatedly stated that EU funds will not cover the costs involved.
But some diplomats in member states say that if the EU could share in the cost of installing cameras, watchtowers, and other infrastructure along its external borders, it would free up national budgets and accelerate the process.
EU officials acknowledge that the refugee reception process is blocked at every step, that the limited reception capacity and the overwhelming burden of the immigration authorities in the member states cannot stop refugees from filing their countless asylum applications in the EU countries, and that the EU's refugee reception system is in a near-permanent crisis state, according to the European website EURACTIV.
According to the European Commission, the EU’s Schengen countries received more than 920,000 asylum applications last year, almost half the number of the previous year.
Meanwhile, the EU recorded over 330,000 illegal entry cases last year.
In this context, the summit also agreed on a "principle of subsidiarity" whereby EU countries can return illegal migrants to their countries on the basis of a court ruling in another member state.
In addition, EU leaders reportedly agreed to “increase the use of the concept of safe states,” which would pave the way for the EU to develop a common list.
(Source: Global Times; Author: Liu Ruifei)
Song Taos words in the interview with Nationalist Party Vice-Chairman Xia Li: Welcome Green Camp visit to the mainland under the 92 consensus
During his visit, Xi Liyen, Vice-Chairman of the Chinese Nationalist Party of Taiwan, met with Song Tao, Director of the Chinese Office for Taiwan, and Wang Shuning, Permanent Member of the Central Political Bureau of the Communist Party of China.
Zhao Chunshan, senior advisor to the Nationalist Party’s official State Policy Foundation, was interviewed by the Taiwan Central News Agency last night, and gave a positive evaluation of Song’s statement that as long as the Green Camp members agree with the “Consensus of 1992” and are against Taiwan’s independence, China welcomes them to visit the mainland.
The National Party has considered it a fresh development.
The news of the day of the meeting between Xi and Song did not mention this statement.
The ruling Democratic Progressive Party of Taiwan has repeatedly clarified its refusal to accept the “Consensus of 2005.”
According to the Central News Agency today, the Nationalist Party Vice-Chairman Xi Liyen led a delegation to Lu, during which time in Beijing, separately met with the Communist Party of China Central Political Bureau Permanent Member Wang Shuning, the new Director of the National Taiwan Office Song Tao, and with the Beijing City Committee Secretary Yun Li.
In an interview with Song Tao, Xi Liyen said that the political basis of the Communist Party of China was the "Consensus of 92" and anti-Taiwan independence, while Zhao Chunshan, a senior adviser to the Nationalist Party's State Policy Foundation, said that the Nationalist Party's "Consensus of 92" was the true "Consensus of 92".
Zhao Chunshan analyzed that this felt different from the previous meetings he had attended.
Recent video interviews with academics from the mainland, as well as this one, did not hear scholars from Taiwan talk about the unity of the military and the “anti-secession law,” but instead about the resumption of exchanges and dialogue.
Liu Chunhan pointed out that the two sides are at risk of a bloody war and that mainland China hopes to communicate its intention to improve relations through the Kuomintang.
Because there is no mutual trust between the CPC and the other party, the latter is still willing to work well for the Taiwanese, and the delegate does not want to damage relations between the two sides.
According to Zhao Chunshan, Wang Shuning also personally instructed Song Tao to say, “They (Taiwan farmers and fishermen) have made demands, you must implement them,” and if they cannot be resolved in a comprehensive way, they will be dealt with on a case-by-case basis.
The report did not mention whether the Nationalist Party delegation visiting the mainland directly referred to the daily overflights of Chinese military aircraft and warships, the agricultural and fisheries problems in Taiwan's few counties and cities, or whether the Central News Agency reporters were interviewed to raise such issues.
What exactly is the asteroid that was shot down over Alaska?
Confusing and contradictory, speculation rife.
On Friday afternoon (10 February), the United States military again used the most advanced American stealth jet fighter F-22 to shoot down an unidentified object flying over Alaska, United States.
The landing site was ten miles off the coast of Alaska.
This was the second time in less than a week that the US forces shot down an aerial flying object.
Last Saturday, a spy balloon from China was shot down off the coast of South Carolina, several days after drifting over US airspace.
The Pentagon said the second object, which first entered U.S. airspace on Thursday night, was tracked by the U.S. military as it moved over northeastern Alaska, flying at an altitude of 12,000 meters (40,000 feet), was about the size of a small car and much smaller than the Chinese spy balloon that was shot down earlier.
The Pentagon also believes that there is no indication that the object is currently capable of being manipulated.
John Corby, the White House National Security Council's Strategic Communications Coordinator, said on Friday that while the exact appearance of the high-altitude object was not clear, it "posed a reasonable threat to the safety of civil aviation."
According to Kobe, the object is different from the spy balloon found in the United States, as it does not have a suspended canister of a payload.
Corby said, "We call it an 'object' is the best description we can make at the moment."
President Biden listened to the Pentagon’s advice before ordering the object to be shot down, and he was “very careful” in making that decision, Corby added.
The official description of the object in the United States can be roughly summarized as: It was the size of a small car, without a handlebar, no suspension, and was flying at an altitude of about 10,000 meters.
However, this information does not answer basic questions such as what the object is, to which country it belongs and what mission it is carrying out.
Currently, much of the analysis and speculation online suggests that this may be another Chinese balloon.
It may have come from China, as did the spy balloon that invaded US airspace and the Chinese balloon that hovered over Latin America, both of which were performing a mission in different locations.
Some have also linked the Alaskan "object" to "unidentified flying objects" (UFOs).
The US News & World Report quoted former US Congressman Peter Meijer as tweeting on Friday that "I hope that the 'UFO' was a spy balloon, not a legitimate UFO."
The irony of Liu confusing alien spacecraft with weather balloons is surprising, but it doesn't deserve to trigger an interstellar conflict, Liu Meijer said.
The tweet was posted shortly after Kobe confirmed that the object in Alaska had been shot down.
The Newsweek said that it was not only Mejer who suspected the object was a UFO.
Republican Rep. Tim Burchett from Tennessee criticized the government’s cover-up last month, calling on the Office of the Director of National Intelligence (DNI) to publish a report on “unidentified flying objects.”
Xi Jinping Receives Letter From Members Of China-Africa Medical Team To Encourage Them To Benefit Local People With Kindness And Practical Actions - Hunan Daily News Network - Huasheng Online
Xi Jinping's letter to the members of the Chinese medical team in Africa to help them tell the story of China through action
February 11, 2023 at 1:09 PM [Source: Xinhua News Agency] [Editor: Li Sufeng] Font size: 【large medium small】
Xinhua Beijing, Feb. 10 (Xinhua) -- General Secretary, President and Chairman of the Central Military Commission of the Communist Party of China (CPC), Xi Jinping, on February 9 replied to the Chinese medical team members of the 19th aid mission to the Central African Republic, sending greetings and expressing his best wishes to them and to the vast medical team.
In response, Xi Jinping said that you in Central Africa, who overcome the difficulties of working life and serve the local people with all your heart, are both angels in white who save the dead and the wounded and friendly messengers of good wishes.
This year marks the 60th anniversary of the dispatch of the Chinese medical team to aid foreign countries. I would like to extend my sincere condolences to the comrades who are currently and have been carrying out medical aid missions abroad.
Xi Jinping said that the Chinese people love peace and value life, and medical aid from abroad is a vivid expression of this.
I hope that you will not forget your original purpose and mission, and will strive to promote the spirit of the Chinese medical team, which is fearless, willing to sacrifice, to save lives, to help injured people and to show unlimited love, and that you will benefit the local people with your kindness and skill, tell the story of China through practical action, and make a greater contribution to promoting the building of a community of human health and health.
Medical assistance is an important part of our foreign aid work.
In 1963, China sent its first medical team abroad to Algeria.
Over the past 60 years, China has dispatched 30,000 medical teams to 76 countries and regions in Africa, Asia, the Americas, Europe and Oceania, treating 290 million patients, and winning the international community &apos; s recognition.
Currently, the medical teams are working in 115 medical facilities in 56 countries around the world, with almost half of them in remote and difficult areas.
Recently, 11 members of the 19th batch of Chinese Medical Team in Central Africa wrote to Xi Jinping, the General Secretary, to report on their experience in implementing the 20th spirit of the Party and providing medical services to local people, expressing their determination to contribute to the building of a community of human health and health.
Iran celebrates anniversary of revolution Hackers who support protests shock president's TV speech
The Islamic Republic of Iran held an official rally on Saturday to mark the 44th anniversary of the Iranian revolution, but anti-government hackers briefly interrupted President Ibrahim Raisi’s television address.
The president's live television address was interrupted on the Internet for about a minute, with a logo of a group of anti-Iranian government hackers named "Edalat Ali" appearing on the screen.
The voice of the Muslim Brotherhood in the country was also heard shouting "Death to the Islamic Republic".
According to Reuters reports today, Iran is commemorating the anniversary of the revolution, and hackers have interrupted the national television coverage.
The Iranian authorities mark the 44th anniversary of the Iranian Revolution, and while the hardline government of Reiss faces the biggest challenge yet from young protesters demanding their removal, Reiss still calls on the deceived youth to repent so that they can be pardoned by Iran's supreme leader.
The wave of nationwide protests continues in Iran after the death of 22-year-old Mahsa Amini in September in the custody of the country's moral police.
The deadly crackdown on protests by Iranian security forces is one of the biggest challenges facing the Islamic Republic since the 1979 revolution that toppled the 2,500-year-old monarchy.
As part of an amnesty to commemorate the anniversary of the revolution, Iranian authorities released imprisoned dissidents Fahad Mesami and Iranian-French scholar Fariba Adelha on Friday for their hunger strike protests.
Earlier, Supreme Leader Ayatollah Ali Khamenei issued an amnesty that included some of the prisoners arrested during recent anti-government protests.
According to the report of Human Rights Activists Network (HRANA), as of Friday, 528 protesters have been killed, including 71 minors.
The report said that 70 other government security personnel were killed.
As many as 19,763 protesters were believed to have been arrested.
For weeks, Iranian leaders and the official media have been calling for voting at Saturday &apos; s rallies to show opposition to the protests and support for the Government.
On Friday evening of the 40th anniversary of the Iranian Revolution, official media showed fireworks as part of a government-sponsored celebration, with people shouting “Allahu Akbar!”
(God is the greatest!)
However, many people at the rally were also heard shouting "Death to the dictator!"
The video of the death of the Islamic Republic of Iran in the city of Qamishli, in the south of the country, was posted on social media.
On Saturday, Government television broadcast live video of the official gatherings in the states throughout the country.
In Tehran, as part of the official celebrations, domestically produced anti-ballistic missiles, drones, anti-submarine cruisers and other military equipment were displayed.
Liesley’s speeches are frequently interrupted by “get out of America,” which is the hallmark slogan at state rallies.
The crowd continued to shout, "Israel, die!"
Adelkhah, who has been in prison since 2019, is one of seven French nationals detained in Iran, Reuters said, a factor in the deterioration of relations between Paris and Tehran in recent months.
She was sentenced to five years in prison in 2020 for national security offences.
They then put her under house arrest at home, but in January she was returned to prison.
Adelkhah denies the accusations.
A week before his release, Mesami’s supporters warned that he was at risk of death as a result of his hunger strike protests.
He was arrested in 2018 for protesting the mandatory wearing of the headscarf.
The French Foreign Ministry responded to Adelkhah's release on Friday, calling for her freedom to be restored, including the possibility of her being allowed to return to France if she wishes.
