The 16th China-Japan Energy Saving and Environmental Integrated Forum in Beijing, where Mr. Ho Lifeng attended the main forum and delivered the keynote address - China News Network
Xinhua Beijing, February 11th, 2017 The 16th China-Japan Energy Saving and Environmental Integrated Forum was held in Beijing on February 11th, 2017 in a combined online and offline format.
The members of the Politburo of the CPC Central Committee, the head of the National Development and Reform Commission, Anyang Lifeng attended the main forum and gave a keynote speech.
Mr. Ho noted that the holding of the Forum is an important initiative to implement the consensus reached in the Bangkok meeting between President Xi Jinping and Prime Minister Fumio Kishida and to strengthen China-Japan cooperation on green development.
China will fully implement the spirit of the 20th Congress of the Communist Party of China, accelerate the green transformation of development methods, make great strides in combating environmental pollution, comprehensively strengthen resource conservation, actively and steadily promote carbon neutrality to the highest level, and promote carbon reduction, pollution reduction, greening and growth in synergy, as well as ecological priority, energy-efficiency and green low-carbon development.
China is willing to continue to deepen cooperation in green, low-carbon industry, technology cooperation, policy dialogue and human exchange with Japan, and to promote green development cooperation between the two countries to a new level.
Japanese Minister of Economy, Trade and Industry Shunji Watanabe attended the main forum and delivered a keynote speech.
The forum was organized by the National Development and Reform Commission of China, the Ministry of Commerce, the Ministry of Economic Affairs and Industry of Japan and the Japan-China Economic Association. It included a main forum and four sub-forums on energy efficiency, intelligent automobile electrification, hydrogen energy and China-Japan long-term trade.
Representatives of Chinese and Japanese governments, enterprises and institutions exchanged views.
Q&A: How to view the U.S. January non-farm employment data greatly exceeded expectations and future trends - Economic Observation Network - Professional financial news website
Q: How do you view the January non-farm employment data in the United States, which exceeded expectations, and the future trends?
A: On February 3, the US Department of Labor released non-farm employment data for January 2023, which showed a new non-farm employment of 517,000, much higher than the market’s expectation of 189,000; the unemployment rate fell to 3.4%, the lowest in almost 50 years; and hourly wages increased by 4.4% year-on-year, and by 0.3% year-on-year, a slight slowdown.
From a total perspective, this data is subject to many one-off and technical factors of disturbance, such as teachers returning from strike, adjustments in survey statistics, updates on seasonal adjustment factors, etc., which may be revised (refer to the downward revision of non-farm payroll employment for January 2022 from 5.04 million to 3.64 million). Non-farm payroll employment may not be as strong as it appears in the data.
Structurally, the impact of the layoffs in high-tech companies remains, but is small; the high-contact service sectors such as leisure hotels, education and healthcare have seen a significant recovery in new jobs, and data show that the labor gap in the service sector remains.
Combined with a similarly over-expected recovery in the services PMI, job vacancy and labor gap data, and strong consumer credit data, we judge that the US services sector is recovering rapidly after extreme weather and holidays.
We believe that the supply-demand tensions in the US job market will not improve without a recession.
There are currently more than 5 million supply gaps in the US labor market, and labour-force participation is rising slowly, especially among the 25-54-year-olds, whose participation is close to its pre-pandemic peak.
In addition, stronger consumer demand will further delay the impact of austerity on the job market due to the strength of the over-saving and consumer credit of the US population.
The continuing tight supply and demand in the US job market will be the foundation of the US economy in 2023.
In addition, with the interest rate hikes now nearing their end and inflation expectations repeating themselves, we are not optimistic about the continued slowdown in wage growth.
Before the data was released, the US equity and bond markets were overly optimistic about the Fed's path to rate hikes.
As inflation data continues to improve, the Fed is slowing its rate hikes while maintaining a fragile balance of market inflation expectations. But markets are ignoring the Fed’s hawk-like statements, expecting not only an early halt to the hikes, but two rate cuts at the end of the year.
In the context of tight labour market supply and demand and uncertain effects of austerity policy, we believe that the Fed's guidance for interest rate hikes at the end of the year is relatively reasonable, and that the extreme market expectations of adjustment and trade congestion will cause some damage to the market.
However, the persistence of wage growth will not reverse the current rapidly declining trend in inflation. As M2 data turns negative year-on-year and the leading indicators of the various CPI sub-elements gradually improve, the US CPI data has moved into a rapidly declining phase since October, the persistence of wage growth will only form a base for future inflation data, and the current market expectations are difficult to falsify, and the market will enter a new round of play after the next inflation data is released.
Shenzhen: Building the First and World's Leading High-Speed City-China News Network
According to the Shenzhen Industrial News and WeChat publicity No. 10 of February, the Shenzhen Municipal Industry and Information Bureau recently published the Shenzhen City's Action Plan for the Construction of a Fast-paced Pioneering City.
It is proposed that by the end of 2023, a super broadband network with high rates, large capacity, and low latency will be built to achieve the goal of “Dual Gigabit, Full Optical Network, 1 millisecond, Everything Connected,” making it China’s first and world-leading city in terms of ultra-fast speed.
The Plan proposes to accelerate the upgrade of the gigabit optical network.
By the end of 2023, the share of 10G PON ports will reach 100%, and the number of all-optical industrial parks (industrial parks) will exceed 100.
The Plan calls for a comprehensive improvement in the energy efficiency of 5G networks.
The research will be conducted to develop the 5G network service quality standards in Shenzhen, conduct 5G network test and evaluation, and improve the quality of 5G network services.
Supporting basic telecommunications enterprises to increase efforts to optimize the 5G network in priority regions and locations, adding 10,000 new 5G base stations throughout the year, the average download speed in the city reached 500Mbps, the upload speed reached 100Mbps, the download speed in the priority areas reached 1000Mbps, the upload speed reached 200Mbps, and the network speed and user experience were significantly improved.
The project aims to build a high-quality wireless local area network at the city level.
Developing wireless local area network (WLAN) service specifications for public places, promoting the upgrade of WLANs in areas with high population density and concentrated information consumption needs throughout the city, and providing gigabyte access capacity.
Based on “Deep iNet”, a unified authentication and supervision platform for public wireless local area networks across the city is being constructed to achieve one-time authentication with seamless roaming and intelligent switching, supporting operators to integrate social self-built APs (wireless access points) with the authentication supervision platform.
By the end of 2023, the total number of upgraded access APs will be at least 20,000.
In addition, the plan also proposes to build a high-quality all-photovoltaic power network, build a multi-level power supply system, accelerate the construction of critical communications network facilities, and improve the Internet application service capability.
The Plan is clear, collaborative building of the system of object-connected perception.
The city will explore the possibility of building a management model for the construction of urban sensing terminals based on the "open source Hongmon" operating system, reducing the cost of connection, accelerating the construction of a city-level IoT sensing platform, and promoting the urban IoT platform, the network of professional IoT platforms in various fields, and the data interconnection.
Deepen the application of IoT sensing in the fields of urban management, public services, public safety, transportation and travel, and expand the collection of fixed sensing data in urban roads, buildings, public facilities and mobile sensing data in smart connected cars.
By the end of 2023, the number of hydroelectric IoT sensor terminals will exceed 9 million, and 20 multifunctional smart pole application demonstration projects will be built.
The plan also mentions the strengthening of satellite and ground communications integration applications, the development of low-air network infrastructure, and the advancement of deep coverage of 5G networks at sea.
At the same time, it will promote deep coverage of the 5G network at sea, build an ecosystem for industrial innovation and development, and support the organization of top-level events and events.
(China New Finance)
China’s e-commerce industry is witnessing “new variables,” how to achieve “content supremacy”?
- China News Network
China News Network, February 11, 2012. Subject: China’s e-commerce industry is emerging as a “new variable,” and how can content be king?
China New Financial Reporter Shaping
We started our e-commerce journey late, but we realized from the beginning that content is important if we want to stand out from the millions of stores.
Fangfang, an 90s girl from Guangdong who runs a health food store on Douyin e-commerce, has made her offline business that has been around for over three decades blossom online.
The video, which is a mimic of the soundtrack of a Hong Kong film, accompanied by classic Cantonese songs, opens the @FangFang one-man-show account on Twitch, and the beautiful video is refreshing to the ears.
At the recent Xiong'an e-commerce forum for the search for peers and sharing of quality content, Fangfang spoke as a representative of quality creators, presenting his experiences and experiences of daily creation.
She said: "The video of my mother's carefully polished food has attracted a lot of attention from netizens, many people are interested in my food and want to make a meal with me, and sales are open".
Translation requested.
Fung Fong has been known to make more people fall in love with the taste of her cooking videos, and one live broadcast sold up to 300,000 nutritious ingredients, saving her family's old store from bankruptcy.
“No content, no e-commerce.” As short videos and live e-commerce continue to evolve, the demands and standards for e-commerce content are entering a new phase.
In the early days of livestreaming, the only selling point seemed to be the price advantage, with livestreamers often offering low-priced discounts to attract customers.
In recent years, phenomenal Vs like Liu Huhong and East Select, as well as many unfamiliar experts and businesses that have emerged in the vertical segmentation field, have been continuously creating high-quality content that fits their brand tone to improve long-term business results.
Gao Yaxun, the chief operating officer of the TikTok e-commerce star author, said that in the past year, 6.27 million creators have made content through TikTok e-commerce, their content creation volume has increased by 252%, and the total transaction amount has more than doubled.
Behind these numbers, we can feel a vibrant, growing author ecosystem with a lot of vitality.
High Sky轩 said.
The Beijing Teachers University Communication Innovation and Future Media Experimental Platform has previously published the E-commerce Industry Content Ecological Health Index (ECHI) report, which analyzes the importance of quality content as a "new variable" in the current e-commerce industry from a data perspective.
According to the report on e-commerce industry content ecosystem health index rankings, Douyin E-commerce, Kuaishou, Tmall, Pinduoduo, and JD rank among the top five.
The report concludes that the content ecosystem of the e-commerce industry is a comprehensive concept that integrates e-commerce with content, but not all content can be integrated with e-commerce, and that good PGC (professional produced content) and UGC (user-generated content) are the quality carriers for integration with e-commerce, and that the higher the value of the content platform, the richer the scenarios for consumption and promotion, the greater the possibility of e-commerce implantation, the stronger the commercial value, and the higher the proportion of e-commerce content production and content consumption that is distributed in this gradually integrated public and private domain.
On-site, Professor Yu Guoming of Beijing Normal University’s School of Journalism and Communication, who is also chairman of the China Media Economics and Management Professional Committee, provided an analysis and interpretation of the report.
He said that in terms of content value, the current e-commerce industry has transitioned from “accessibility to consumption” to “quality-oriented consumption,” and high-quality, professional, and differentiated content is the “hard currency” of the e-commerce industry.
At the same time, content has become the foundation and the catch of the new phase of e-commerce development, and PGC content such as knowledge payment, professional knowledge, KOL (key opinion leader) has begun to become standard in e-commerce live broadcast.
Looking ahead to the future development of the e-commerce industry, Hu Guoming makes two recommendations.
One is to promote the overall improvement of the ecological health of e-commerce content and quality from the perspective of improving the content structure, to create positive content creation and management standards, and to achieve the index of the e-commerce industry's content ecological health system and dynamic balance.
The other is the synergy and co-creation of values from an external ecological perspective to achieve the healthy development of the content e-commerce industry and the external environment.
The future e-commerce industry also needs more data and AI support to form predictions about the future stability of development; In addition, to provide more regulations and healthy growth space for businessmen, to achieve synergy of values of enterprises, users, products and services in the e-commerce industry, and to co-create a healthy content ecosystem.
