Not very recommended reading
I read it a long time ago and I happened to see the feeling of reading it from memory.
Rather than a collection of short stories, the book is a collection of fragments of life about love.
The tone of this book is extremely plain; it’s like drinking water – bland and unassuming. The language used is minimalist to an extreme degree, with every word chosen for its impact on the reader. The plot is as quiet and unassuming as a summer afternoon in the city streets.
Each short story is a silhouette of a small period in ordinary life, without beginning or end.
Finally, they were collected together under the title What We Are Talking About When We Talk About Love.
I think that this collection of novels, and its title, is like an act of art, in which the author wants to express that love is more than a tragic union on stage, a dry sea in urban legends, or a cold-blooded one-on-one, that love is more than that and should not be represented by that, but that it is also a life of watery plains, a dull day after day, but also a life of helplessness, an escape from reality, and uncertainty about the future.
You may be reading this book with couples arguing next to you, people you know whose marriages have been a mess, and feelings that are not what you want.
This is exactly why I don't recommend reading it, from an aesthetic point of view, the writing and the plot of the book are completely tasteless, unless your life is a surreal or sweet as living in a candy castle, you have to read it to feel weird and boring.
And, in terms of thought depth, the everyday plot does not brighten or expand one’s mind (unlike Marx’s Love in the Age of Cholera), and the short clips do not address any questions, such as what mistakes lead to failed love?
What causes the breakdown of the protagonist's marriage?
I don't recommend reading this book, it doesn't make much sense not to read it.
The author's ideas are expressed more through technique and body style than plot, which is also the reason why the reading experience is so poor.
